WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.010
Hi, Bob the Canadian here.

2
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.000
As you continue to learn English,

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.440
you want to be able to talk
about your daily routine.

4
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.110
In this English lesson, I
will invite you along with me

5
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.030
for part of my day so that
you can see my daily routine

6
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.170
and along the way, you'll be able

7
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.540
to learn how to talk
about your daily routine.

8
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.870
So in this video, we'll go
from the moment I wake up

9
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.600
until about the end of my work day.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.100
This is part one of two videos
where you're going to learn

11
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.893
to talk about your daily routine.

12
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.010
The very first thing I do every day

13
00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:50.090
is I wake up and then I usually press

14
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.390
the snooze button on my alarm clock.

15
00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.840
When you wake up, it means you go from

16
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.080
being asleep to being awake,

17
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.040
but when my alarm first goes off,

18
00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.300
I usually wanna sleep
just a little bit more.

19
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.853
So I'm gonna do that right now.

20
00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.580
So the second thing I do
in the morning is I get up.

21
00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.500
When you get up, it means
you actually get out of bed.

22
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.933
So I think it's time for me to get up.

23
00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.010
The first thing I like
to do after I get up

24
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.660
is I like to make the bed.

25
00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.600
It's always nice when
you have your bed made.

26
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.740
So after I get up and
after I make the bed,

27
00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.300
I usually use the bathroom.

28
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.390
This room behind me is our bathroom

29
00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.050
and in English you can
say this a number of ways.

30
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.800
You can say, "I use the bathroom,"

31
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.630
you can say, "I go to the bathroom,"

32
00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.890
you can also in Canadian English
say, "I use the washroom,"

33
00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.920
or, "I go to the washroom."

34
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.520
This is the one part of the lesson though

35
00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.560
where I'm not taking the camera with me.

36
00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.513
I'll be right back.

37
00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.580
So the next thing I do
every day is make breakfast.

38
00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:04.300
I usually fry two eggs in a frying pan,

39
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:09.300
I usually make myself two
pieces of toast in the toaster,

40
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.850
and I make myself a mug of coffee.

41
00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:16.640
That is a pretty standard
Bob the Canadian breakfast.

42
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.970
So after I make breakfast,
I eat breakfast.

43
00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.530
There's actually two ways to
say this, though, in English.

44
00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.750
You can say, "I eat breakfast,"

45
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.360
but you can also say, "I have breakfast."

46
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.850
So I eat my egg on toast

47
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.400
and I drink my coffee
from my favorite mug.

48
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.110
This actually says, "Love
the World, Bob the Canadian."

49
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.980
This is from a friend
of mine named Miroslav.

50
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.330
Thanks again Miroslav for the mug.

51
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:45.330
But again, every day I eat
breakfast or I have breakfast.

52
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.810
The next thing I do is I use my computer

53
00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.810
to check my email and to read the news.

54
00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.340
I like to check my email every morning

55
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.910
and I like to read the news every morning.

56
00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.990
I also spend a little bit of time

57
00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.160
checking my social media accounts

58
00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.560
like Facebook and Instagram and TikTok.

59
00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.340
I probably spend a little
bit too much time doing that.

60
00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.700
So this next part of my
day you are not invited to

61
00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.880
because every day I take a shower.

62
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.210
There are two ways to say
this, though, in English.

63
00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.860
You can say, "Every day I take a shower."

64
00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.310
You can also say, "Every
day I have a shower."

65
00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:25.600
I usually take a shower every
day before I go to work.

66
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.480
After my shower, I dry off with a towel

67
00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.140
and then I put on some deodorant.

68
00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.840
After that, I get dressed.

69
00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.800
I decide what I'm going
to wear for the day

70
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.460
and then I get dressed and
I get ready to go to work.

71
00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.170
After I get dressed, I
go back to the bathroom

72
00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.180
and if I need to, I will shave,

73
00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.820
but I don't actually shave every day.

74
00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.990
But if it's a day where
I need to shave, I shave.

75
00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.010
After that, I get some
toothpaste and my toothbrush

76
00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.300
and I will brush my teeth.

77
00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.010
So the next thing I do is
I come back to the kitchen

78
00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.290
and I make a lunch.

79
00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.560
I don't like to buy lunch every day.

80
00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.490
I don't like to spend money.

81
00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:09.000
So I usually make a sandwich
and I grab a banana,

82
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.720
and this will be my lunch for today.

83
00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.520
So in English, we would say,
"Every day I make a lunch."

84
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.230
We can also, though, say,
"Every day I pack a lunch."

85
00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.600
When you pack a lunch, it means that you

86
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.820
put your lunch in a nice
lunch bag like this one.

87
00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:28.450
So every day I make a lunch,
and every day I pack a lunch.

88
00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.300
The next thing I do every
day is I grab my things.

89
00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:36.050
When I say I grab my things,
it means that I grab my keys,

90
00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:40.940
I grab my phone, I grab my
wallet, I grab my laptop,

91
00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.900
and I grab the lunch that I
made because I'm just about

92
00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.520
ready to head out the door and go to work.

93
00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.360
So the next thing I do in my
daily routine is I go to work.

94
00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:56.360
Every day at about 7:30 Monday
through Friday, I go to work.

95
00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.910
If you were someone who
was in school though,

96
00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.500
you would say, "I go to school."

97
00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.810
If you are someone who stays home,

98
00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:08.090
at this point in your
routine you might stay home.

99
00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:12.070
But for me, every day at
this time, I go to work.

100
00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:14.350
One of the things I like
about my drive to work

101
00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:17.240
is that there are no traffic jams, ever.

102
00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.120
It takes me only 10 minutes to drive

103
00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:22.390
from my house to the
school that I work at.

104
00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:26.460
When I get to work, I take off my jacket

105
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.053
and I hang up my jacket,

106
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.640
and then I say hi to all the other

107
00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.240
teachers in the staffroom.

108
00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.870
Hi everybody.

109
00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:36.703
Hi.

110
00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:37.536
Hi, Bob.

111
00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.823
I put my lunch in the fridge,

112
00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:44.440
I teach my first class of the day,

113
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.520
which is grade nine French,
this is our textbook,

114
00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:50.340
to a lot of students who are usually

115
00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:53.297
very interested in
learning a new language.

116
00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.190
Every day after teaching my first class,

117
00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.490
I go to my teacher work area

118
00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.440
and I grade student work with my red pen

119
00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:08.720
and I plan my lessons
for my next two classes.

120
00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.490
After that it's lunch time,

121
00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.530
so I eat my lunch and I
talk to the other teachers

122
00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:17.430
who are in the staffroom
eating their lunch as well.

123
00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.920
Hey, did you see that
hockey game the other night?

124
00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.410
I know this doesn't sound very Canadian

125
00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.980
but I don't actually watch hockey.

126
00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.520
After lunch, I teach my
next class of the day,

127
00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.040
which is computer class.

128
00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.700
In computer class, I teach
students how to make video games.

129
00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.080
It is a really, really fun class.

130
00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.220
And then I teach my last class of the day,

131
00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.630
which is grade 10 French.

132
00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.193
This is our textbook.

133
00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:47.600
And that's pretty much
the end of my workday.

134
00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.580
I usually put on my jacket
at the end of the day

135
00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.560
and I say bye, bye everybody,
to all of my colleagues.

136
00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.100
Well hey, thanks for coming along

137
00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.420
with me for part of my day.

138
00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.410
I hope you were able to learn

139
00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.500
a few more English words and phrases

140
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.040
to talk about your daily routine.

141
00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.720
Don't forget that next week,

142
00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:07.880
part two of this video will come out

143
00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.980
where I will talk some more about

144
00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:12.330
the things that I normally
do in the evening.

145
00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.300
But I hope this English lesson

146
00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.340
helped you learn just a few
more English words and phrases

147
00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.610
to talk about your daily routines.

148
00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:22.260
I'm Bob the Canadian and you're
learning English with me.

149
00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:24.650
Don't forget to subscribe
if you are new here

150
00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.780
and give me a thumbs up if this video

151
00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.930
helped you learn just a
little bit more English.

152
00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:30.856
Thanks for watching and have a great day.
